-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- The table headed "Acts Referred to" that the rendering prints before the text of the Act: eighteen rows, each a title and, for fourteen of them,
-- the citation printed beside it (the calendar year and consecutive number, or the regnal year and chapter). It is a table of citations and states no
-- rule of the Act; the rendering places it with the arrangement of sections, outside the numbered text. It is encoded as a lookup so that the citation
-- of an Act the text names can be read from the Act's own table, and so that section 14(1)(b) and (c) (how an Act may be cited) have the Act's examples.
-- Four rows (the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998, the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001, the Social Welfare Acts and the Survey (Ireland) Acts 1825 to 1870) are
-- collective citations with nothing printed beside them; the lookup returns NOTHING for their citation, which is the table's own silence.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Types`

